cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "promptdiff: Lightweight Comparison Utilities for LLM Prompt Strings"
authors:
  - family-names: Deshmukh
    given-names: Vaibhav
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-04-27"
url: "https://github.com/vdeshmukh203/promptdiff"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vdeshmukh203/promptdiff"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - prompt engineering
  - large language models
  - text comparison
  - diff
  - similarity
abstract: >
  promptdiff is a pure-Python, zero-dependency library for comparing LLM
  prompt strings. It provides a line-aware structured diff, a unified-diff
  formatter, and a character-bigram cosine similarity score, together with
  a Tkinter-based GUI and a command-line interface.
